@* A win rate as a bar and a figure — the "Win rate" column of the three statistics tables.

   The fill is WinTone's, not a threshold of its own: the class ladder here used to be a second
   copy of "green from 50% up" with a comment promising it would be kept in step, and it had
   already slipped a step lighter on the losing side than the same bar on the landing page.

   The empty state is the component's rather than the caller's. All three tables gated the bar on
   "has anything finished?" and wrote the dash out themselves, in three copies of the same three
   lines; a rate over nothing but drafts is 0 by arithmetic, and a full-width ember bar would
   report a run of defeats that never happened. *@

@if (Completed > 0)
{
    <div class="flex min-w-[140px] items-center gap-3">
        <Meter Value="Pct" FillColor="@WinTone.FillFor(Pct, Completed)" Class="flex-1"/>
        <span class="w-9 text-right text-xs tabular-nums text-ink-700">@($"{Pct:F0}%")</span>
    </div>
}
else
{
    <span class="no-figure text-xs">—</span>
}

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public double Pct { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Finished games behind the rate. Zero draws the dash instead of the bar — see above.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public int Completed { get; set; }
}
